## Supplementary Table S8. Colocalisation of total-body BMD with knee OA at all 31 instrument loci

Regions are ±500 kb around each strict-clumped total-body BMD instrument. PP.H0–PP.H4 are posterior probabilities under priors p1=p2=1×10⁻⁴, p12=5×10⁻⁶. No locus reaches PP.H4≥0.8; six favour distinct causal variants (PP.H3≥0.8). The highest single-locus PP.H4 was 0.799 (rs11228269, chr11:68.29 Mb; BMD z=−8.65, knee-OA z=−4.06, direction-concordant; PP.H1=0.156), i.e. one locus fell 0.0006 short of the threshold; the pre-specified 0.8 cut-off is retained. (Full locus-level table in the repository; see Data availability.)

